WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.391 --> 00:00:03.075
An AI agent in Attis sets up cluster

2
00:00:03.075 --> 00:00:04.437
search from your description.

3
00:00:05.719 --> 00:00:07.882
Cluster search has dozens of settings,

4
00:00:08.042 --> 00:00:10.526
like volume type, position in the bar,

5
00:00:10.526 --> 00:00:12.929
and candle direction. Building your own

6
00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:15.093
pattern from them by hand takes a long

7
00:00:15.093 --> 00:00:17.857
time. The agent only needs the pattern

8
00:00:17.857 --> 00:00:20.661
described in words. Cell absorption, for

9
00:00:20.661 --> 00:00:23.505
example. Heavy selling in the lower

10
00:00:23.505 --> 00:00:25.909
wick of the bar, yet the bar still closes

11
00:00:25.909 --> 00:00:28.553
up. How many of these a day checked over

12
00:00:28.553 --> 00:00:31.407
the past week?The agent adds the

13
00:00:31.407 --> 00:00:34.211
indicator, sets the volume type, position

14
00:00:34.211 --> 00:00:36.334
in the bar and candle direction itself,

15
00:00:36.655 --> 00:00:39.619
and tunes the threshold to your data. The

16
00:00:39.619 --> 00:00:41.782
chart now marks the spots that match your

17
00:00:41.782 --> 00:00:44.747
description. It checked the settings day

18
00:00:44.747 --> 00:00:46.870
by day and showed how many marks it

19
00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:49.474
found. And it listed the filters it

20
00:00:49.474 --> 00:00:52.198
set. Keep them or adjust them. It's your

21
00:00:52.198 --> 00:00:54.481
call. An imbalance,

22
00:00:54.642 --> 00:00:56.564
absorption, or your own footprint

23
00:00:56.564 --> 00:00:59.128
pattern. The agent turns the description

24
00:00:59.128 --> 00:01:01.892
into settings. Connect an AI agent to

25
00:01:02.013 --> 00:01:04.656
Atas and try it out. You choose the agent

26
00:01:04.656 --> 00:01:06.179
and its subscription yourself.

27
00:01:10.024 --> 00:01:12.148
Imagine it. Atas does it.
